1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:04,480
Hamas says it would allegedly release all Israeli hostages in exchange for Palestinians

2
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:06,040
imprisoned by Israel.

3
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:09,880
Even before October 7, Israel was holding more than a thousand Palestinian detainees

4
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:11,320
without charge.

5
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:15,440
Just a few days ago, Israel detained thousands of Gazans who are lawfully working in Israel

6
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:16,600
with work permits.

7
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:21,640
According to Gisha, an Israeli NGO whose goal is to protect the freedom of movement of Palestinians,

8
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:23,920
the arrests were made without cause.

9
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:28,240
So now, thousands of Palestinians are incarcerated in Israel without charge or trial.

10
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:31,920
As things tense up, legal advocates and human rights activists are showing that there are

11
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:34,520
a lot of Palestinian hostages on the other side.

12
00:00:34,520 --> 00:00:41,600
At the end of June 2023, the Israel Prison Service was holding 1,117 Palestinians in administrative

13
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:42,600
detention.

14
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:47,360
Beth Selem, an Israeli human rights organization, explains what administrative detention means.

15
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:52,480
It means incarceration without trial or charge, alleging that a person plans to commit a future

16
00:00:52,480 --> 00:00:53,480
offense.

17
00:00:53,480 --> 00:00:57,400
That person faces unknown allegations with no way to disprove them.

18
00:00:57,400 --> 00:01:02,800
Under Israeli law, administrative detention can be extended every six months, without limit.

19
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:07,120
Extensions are reviewed by an Israeli military court, behind closed doors, based on secret

20
00:01:07,120 --> 00:01:09,980
material that is not even disclosed to the defense attorney.

21
00:01:09,980 --> 00:01:14,220
One former judge even admitted in an interview, quote, all my information comes through the

22
00:01:14,220 --> 00:01:16,680
Israeli general security service agents.

23
00:01:16,680 --> 00:01:18,400
I didn't doubt what they said.

24
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:23,340
About 100 percent of all military court cases in the West Bank end in conviction.

25
00:01:23,340 --> 00:01:28,160
Palestinian Prisoner Society reports that 95 percent of Palestinian detainees have suffered

26
00:01:28,160 --> 00:01:28,740
from torture in prison.

27
00:01:28,740 --> 00:01:33,660
We would hear screams from other cells and smell tear gas, but we couldn't tell what was

28
00:01:33,660 --> 00:01:34,660
happening.

29
00:01:34,660 --> 00:01:37,660
Some prisoners would tell us about beatings by Israeli forces.

30
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:40,740
Their hands were broken, and heads and backs were injured.

31
00:01:40,740 --> 00:01:42,620
This is happening to children, too.

32
00:01:42,620 --> 00:01:45,260
Hundreds of Palestinian prisoners are below the age of 18.

33
00:01:45,260 --> 00:01:51,060
In a report from July, kids said that they were violated sexually and put in cages.

34
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:55,940
For scale, the number of Palestinian children in Israeli detention in a single year exceeds

35
00:01:55,940 --> 00:02:01,140
the total number of people held by the U.S. in Guantanamo since 2002.

36
00:02:01,140 --> 00:02:04,980
Palestinians in Israeli prisons are systematically denied family visits and phone calls.

37
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:09,220
There's also overcrowding, and just last week, Israeli parliament approved measures to make

38
00:02:09,220 --> 00:02:11,260
the living spaces even smaller.

39
00:02:11,260 --> 00:02:16,220
According to Military Court Watch, Israel has detained about 800,000 Palestinians since

40
00:02:16,220 --> 00:02:17,540
1967.

41
00:02:17,540 --> 00:02:22,340
But that number is actually just a rough estimate, because actually, Israel doesn't publish clear

42
00:02:22,340 --> 00:02:25,340
or accurate information about Palestinians in custody.

43
00:02:25,340 --> 00:02:29,900
One thing we do know, in the last couple of weeks, Israel has doubled its number of Palestinian

44
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:32,900
prisoners, growing to about 10,000.

45
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:38,780
Al Jazeera reports that since October 7, Israel has arrested 4,000 laborers from Gaza and more

46
00:02:38,780 --> 00:02:40,880
than 1,000 people in the West Bank.

47
00:02:40,880 --> 00:02:44,140
May all civilian hostages on both sides be released.

